\begin{align*}0 &= a\left(x + 2\right)(x - 5)\left(x - 9\right)\left(x + \frac13\right)\\&= \left(3ax + 6a\right)(x - 5)(x - 9)\left(x + \frac13\right)\\&= (3ax + 6a)(x - 5)\left(x^2 - \frac{34}3x - 15\right)\\&= (3ax + 6a)(x^3 - \frac43ax^2 - \frac{179}3x + 75)\end{align*}
Expanding and collecting like terms, we find that $-225a$ is the constant term and $6a$ is the coefficient of $x.$  Thus, the smallest possible positive value of $a$ is $\boxed{15}.$</think> <answer>15</answer>

